In acceptance/test_assign_rooms.py the two tests assert opposite results for the identical input:

  assign_rooms([("sync", 540, 600, 4), ("plan", 540, 600, 5)], {"Atlas": 5, "Borea": 8})

- test_same_start_time expects {"plan": "Atlas", "sync": "Borea"}
- test_regression_issue_667 expects {"sync": "Atlas", "plan": "Borea"}

Per the SLOTPLAN-117 design review, meetings starting at the same minute are handled largest first (more attendees, then meeting_id), so a big meeting is not squeezed out by a smaller one listed before it. That gives {"plan": "Atlas", "sync": "Borea"}. test_regression_issue_667 is therefore the stale/incorrect expectation. The acceptance dir is read-only so I can't fix it. Please update test_regression_issue_667 to match the design review. Implementation in src/slotplan/assign_rooms.py is green on unit tests.

